#
# Review-gate policy, not a contact list. Patterns below define Tier C
# ("touches live infra, credentials, or CI/automation permissions") --
# anything matching requires @jcasnellie69's review via branch protection's
# "Require review from Code Owners". Anything NOT matched here has no
# required review (Tier A/B) and can auto-merge on green CI.
#
# Default posture is deny: unrecognized new paths under deploy/ansible/
# fall under the broad playbooks/ rule below, so a brand-new playbook is
# Tier C by default, not Tier A. Only explicitly-listed, known-safe,
# read-only/check-mode-default playbooks are carved back out.
#
# Ordering matters -- CODEOWNERS uses last-match-wins. Broad Tier C rules
# come first; Tier B carve-outs (no owner) come after so they win.

# --- Tier C: mutation-capable or sensitive by default ---
/deploy/ansible/playbooks/ @jcasnellie69
/deploy/ansible/scripts/ @jcasnellie69
/deploy/ansible/group_vars/ @jcasnellie69
/deploy/ansible/host_vars/ @jcasnellie69
/deploy/ansible/inventory/ @jcasnellie69
/configs/ @jcasnellie69
/.github/workflows/ @jcasnellie69
/.github/CODEOWNERS @jcasnellie69
/ops/systemd/ @jcasnellie69
/CLAUDE.md @jcasnellie69
/LANES.md @jcasnellie69

# --- Tier B carve-outs: known-safe, read-only / check-mode-default ---
